				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/andrewobt" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4115020); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4115020&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238167" alt="AndrewOBT" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4115020)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/andrewobt" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4115020); return false;" >AndrewOBT</a></span> <span class="odate time_1531170179 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">09 Jul 2018 21:02</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3868153">
									

<p>What I got from it was not only &quot;this cannot reach a final resting place or we're screwed&quot; but &quot;we are <em>absolutely</em> following procedure. We'll get to it. Yep. It just&#8230;takes time.&quot;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;spoiler</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;I&nbsp;feel&nbsp;too&nbsp;clever</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>If they put into writing that the containment procedures are that this thing is not to be permanently contained anywhere&#8230;poof. So they have to skirt procedure by saying they <em>are totally going to contain this thing</em> but it already is contained. Sort of. It's complicated. The procrastination might also be an anomalous effect but I don't actually think so.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Yeah, real cool, enjoyed it, +1.</p>

